### Page 7 of 15

```text
UDC-22-00133
May 2, 2022
vacation does not serve as a connection, and utilities utilizing this right-of-way will have
easements provided.

Vacation of the property complies with this criterion.

2) The ability of all existing and potential future development on adjacent lots to meet all
applicable standards for development in the existing zoning district, including other
development options in the event that any specific development proposed in association with
the vacation is not executed after approval  (UDC 2.1.4.d.2).

The proposed vacation is minor and does not substantively change the public-private interface.
The right-of-way was already included as part of the development plan on the adjacent parcel
(as the right-of-way landscaping and access are typically found on site plans for development at
any location in the City). Any future development on the parcel would be required to address
this area (whether private property or public right-of-way).

Vacation of the property complies with this criterion.

3) The vacation reflects sound planning and urban design principles with respect to existing
potential future development in the vicinity, including consideration of current and future
streets, open spaces, blocks and lots, and public utilities or facilities (UDC 2.1.4.d.3).

The proposed vacation does not eliminate any publicly dedicated connections and all public
travel will be retained in the remaining right-of-way. The area to be vacated has utilities, but a
utility easement is proposed to be included with the vacation.

Vacation of the property complies with this criterion.

4) The application meets the public interest, and is not otherwise prohibited by other city, state,
or federal laws (UDC 2.1.4.d.4).

The portion of the right-of-way proposed to be vacated only services one owner (who has
petitioned for the vacation). All north-south public travel is maintained in the remaining right-of-
way.  Allowing the vacation would allow the landowner greater flexibility in the future and
would relieve the City of some maintenance.

Vacation of the property complies with this criterion.

5) The review and recommendations of other reviewing bodies (UDC 2.1.4.d.5).

The Metropolitan Planning Organization recommended that the entire western splinter island
be within right-of-way. However, the proposed splinter island already extends into private
property, and the entirety of the splinter island east of (and including) the public sidewalk will
still be in the right-of-way.

Vacation of the property complies with this criterion.
```

### Page 8 of 15

```text
UDC-22-00133
May 2, 2022
CONFORMANCE WITH APPLICABLE PLANS:

The project is located in an area covered by the following plans:

PlanCheyenne
PlanCheyenne designates this area as Mixed-use Commercial. The Plan also encourages responsiveness
to market demands and the responsible extension of infrastructure. As the infrastructure located in this
roundabout leg is not required for effective maintenance of Sweetgrass Drive, vacation would be more
responsible for City maintenance. The vacation of this area will not adversely impact the ability for this
property to be accessed for commercial uses, and may allow the property more flexibility.

STAFF REVIEW:

Staff review is covered by review criterion #5 (above).

CONCLUSION:

The application meets all the review criteria as filed.

ALTERNATIVES:

1. Recommend approval of the vacation as submitted by the applicant (Staff Recommendation).
2. Recommend approval of the vacation subject to conditions or modifications.
3. Recommend denial of the vacation based on findings of denial. The Planning Commission must
conclude that the project does not meet all the review criteria. As part of the motion, findings
for denial must be stated.
4. Postpone the vacation until issues identified during the meeting can be resolved.

General Information Regarding Alternatives:

In the event that
recommended
conditions of approval, the Commission shall cite specific reasons (based on the review criteria) for approval or
denial.

STAFF RECOMMENDATION:

Staff recommends approval of the vacation.

ATTACHMENTS:
1. Zoning Map
2. Land Use Plan Map
3. Application
4. Formal Petition
5. Applicant-provided Vacation Map
```

